Just to amplify what Simon wrote: Just because you have seen a scroll
of identify, and therefore can identify new scrolls of identify on
sight, has no connection with whether you know what a spellbook of
identify looks like.  Since you've never identified a spellbook of
identify, it is considered unknown to you.

For writing an unknown spellbook, a wizard has a base chance of 1 in
3, non-wizard 1 in 15. It is then modified by luck and luck alone,
with good luck making it more likely to succeed and bad luck making it
less likely. Neither your level nor your intelligence have any affect
on writing it. (They do have an affect on reading it after it's
written, though.)



